// Scoreboard demo on AxiLiteRegs. Fuzz writes random values to MM2S_SA;
// each randomized value is pushed onto a `queue<uint<32>>` in a
// `scoreboard`. After each axil_read, pop the next expected value from
// the queue and compare. End-of-test: queue must be empty.
//
// Spec §8.5: scoreboards are the natural place to compare DUT-observed
// transactions against test-produced expectations. v0 lowers the
// declaration to a C++ struct; the user pushes/pops directly. `on`-
// handlers attached to monitors are deferred (need event registration).

scoreboard FuzzSb
    expected : queue<uint<32>>
    writes : uint<32> default 0    // count of writes pushed
    reads  : uint<32> default 0    // count of reads compared
end scoreboard FuzzSb

transaction FuzzReg
    value : uint<32>
end transaction FuzzReg

test AxiLiteSbTest
    let dut : AxiLiteRegs
end test AxiLiteSbTest
